  "title": "What Sugar Does to Your Teeth (and How Spit Fights Back)",
  "phrase": "what sugar does to your teeth",
  "opener": "What sugar does to your teeth: mouth bacteria turn it into acid, and the acid attacks your enamel until a cavity forms. This cartoon shows it on a tooth cut open. Then Dr. Mira explains the twist: your own spit helps repair enamel, if you snack less often and brush twice a day with fluoride toothpaste.",
  "question": "How many times a day do you snack on something sweet?",
